// A notation staff ABOVE a tab staff of the same music: the tab's forced-above
// Scripts (fermata, flageolet) sit in the inter-staff gap and must NOT collide
// with the notation staff's low noteheads. The gap widens to reserve them.
title "Tab articulations (multi-staff)"
time 4/4
key c major

part m {
  instrument bass
  section A { a4@accent a@flageolet a@fermata a@portato | }
}

form main { A }

score main {
  staff m
  tab m as full
}

// ⚠ THE TAB ASKS FOR `as full` EXPLICITLY (2026-08-29). A tab beside a notation staff
// of the same part now defaults to `as numbers`, which draws no stems, beams, dots,
// tuplet numbers or ties -- and this book is ABOUT one of those, so without the clause
// it would keep passing while testing nothing it claims to.
